#~ msgid "The platform's shell scripts are bash. On Windows they run under Git Bash, which Git for Windows installs, so  is the only extra prerequisite. Every script a user runs by hand or wires into a config has a  beside it — , , ,  and so on — which finds Git Bash (never the WSL launcher in ) and runs the sibling  with the same arguments. Use them from , PowerShell, Task Scheduler or an MCP config entry:"
